            <div class="projects">
                <h3 id="about-title">Projects</h3>
                <!-- 1st project -->
                <div class="main-project">
                    <h3 id="project-name">LEETCODE MATRICS APP</h3>
                    <h2 class="skill-tags html">HTML</h2>
                    <h2 class="skill-tags css">CSS</h2>
                    <h2 class="skill-tags js">JavaScript</h2>
                    <p id="descriptio">LeetMatric is a JavaScript-based web application that fetches and visualizes a user’s LeetCode problem-solving statistics. It uses the LeetCode GraphQL API to display difficulty-wise progress (Easy, Medium, Hard) through interactive circular charts and submission summary cards. This project was built to gain hands-on experience with JavaScript, asynchronous programming, APIs, and frontend–backend interaction using Node.js and Express.</p>
                    <a href="https://github.com/sandeshpawar10/LeetCode-Matrics-App" target="_blank" class="check-it-btn">Check it Out</a>
                </div>

                <!-- 2nd project -->

                <div class="main-project">
                    <h3 id="project-name">MOVIE SEARCH APP</h3>
                    <h2 class="skill-tags html">HTML</h2>
                    <h2 class="skill-tags css">CSS</h2>
                    <h2 class="skill-tags js">JavaScript</h2>
                    <p id="descriptio">The Movie Info Project is a web-based application built using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript that allows users to search for movies and view detailed information in real time. The app fetches data from the TMDB (The Movie Database) API and displays movie details such as title, poster, release date, rating, overview, director, and top cast members. It also includes filters for Hollywood and Bollywood (Indian regional movies), supports search by movie name and year, and provides smooth animations for a better user experience.</p>
                    <a href="https://github.com/sandeshpawar10/Movie-Info-Project" target="_blank" class="check-it-btn">Check it Out</a>
                </div>

                <!-- 3rd project -->

                <div class="main-project">
                    <h3 id="project-name">BOOKSTORE API DRIZZLE</h3>
                    <h2 class="skill-tags node">Node js</h2>
                    <h2 class="skill-tags express">Express</h2>
                    <p id="descriptio">The Bookstore REST API is a backend application built using Node.js, Express, Drizzle ORM, and PostgreSQL, designed to manage books and authors with proper relational database principles. The project implements UUID-based primary keys, foreign key relationships, and referential integrity, ensuring that every book is associated with a valid author.</p>
                    <a href="https://github.com/sandeshpawar10/Bookstore-Api-Drizzle-Project/tree/main" target="_blank" class="check-it-btn">Check it Out</a>
                </div>

                <!-- 4th project -->
                 <div class="main-project">
                    <h3 id="project-name">URL SHORTNER PROJECT</h3>
                    <h2 class="skill-tags html">Node Js</h2>
                    <h2 class="skill-tags css">Express</h2>
                    <h2 class="skill-tags PostgreSQL">PostgreSQL</h2>
                    <h2 class="skill-tags Docker">Docker</h2>
                    <h2 class="skill-tags Validators">Zod Validators</h2>
                    <h2 class="skill-tags Drizzle">Drizzle ORM</h2>
                    <p id="descriptio">I developed a production-ready URL Shortener Backend using Node.js, Express.js, PostgreSQL, and Drizzle ORM that allows users to securely generate and manage shortened URLs with JWT-based authentication and salted password hashing. The project includes RESTful APIs for user registration, login, URL shortening, and redirection, along with relational database design using PostgreSQL foreign key relationships. I also integrated Docker for containerized backend and database setup, used Zod for request validation, and NanoID for generating unique short codes, making the system scalable, secure, and deployment-ready.</p>
                    <a href="https://github.com/sandeshpawar10/URL-Shortner-Project" target="_blank" class="check-it-btn">Check it Out</a>
                </div>

                <!-- 5TH PROJECT -->
                 <div class="main-project">
                    <h3 id="project-name">MOVIE BOOKING WEB APP</h3>
                    <h2 class="skill-tags node">Node js</h2>
                    <h2 class="skill-tags express">Express</h2>
                    <h2 class="skill-tags Mongo">Mongo DB</h2>
                    <h2 class="skill-tags LeafLet">LeafLet</h2>
                    <p id="descriptio">A full-stack Movie Booking System web application that allows users to browse movies, select theatres and show timings, choose seats in real time, and securely book tickets through an integrated online payment gateway. The platform provides a smooth and interactive booking experience with dynamic seat management, user authentication, and admin controls for managing movies and shows. The project is built using modern web technologies with a scalable backend, database integration, and Razorpay payment support, making it a complete real-world cinema ticket booking solution.</p>
                    <a href="https://github.com/sandeshpawar10/Movie-Booking-App/tree/main" target="_blank" class="check-it-btn">Check it Out</a>
                </div>

